course: dictionary
lesson: 15639
title: Special words for special subjects
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Every subject and job has its own special words. Footballers talk about offside and penalties, musicians talk about tempo and crescendo, and doctors use many words that most people never need. The name for this set of special words is terminology.
explain: «The teacher asked us to use the correct terminology in our science report.» Correct terminology means the right special words for the subject. Instead of writing "the green bits of the plant", a scientist would write "chlorophyll", because that is the proper word for the job.
explain: When you learn a subject, you learn its terminology. This helps you understand experts and explain your own ideas clearly. Look for the word in phrases like «technical terminology» and «scientific terminology».
fact: Terminology means the special words and phrases used in a subject or job.
fact: Terminology is uncountable, so you say "the terminology", not "a terminology".
fact: «Numerator» and «denominator» are maths terminology: the top and bottom numbers of a fraction.
fact: «Photosynthesis» is science terminology, and «noun» and «verb» are grammar terminology.
fact: Ordinary words like "happy" or "big" are not terminology, because everyone uses them in everyday life.
exercise: The words numerator and denominator belong to maths. What do we call special words like these? | *Terminology | Rhymes | Slang | Dialect
exercise: «The doctor used the correct terminology to explain the injury.» What does correct terminology mean here? | Silly nicknames for body parts | Words from a different country | *The right special words for medicine | Words that rhyme
exercise: Which word is grammar terminology? | Happy | Blue | Quickly | *Noun
test: «Tempo» and «crescendo» are words from music. What do we call the special words used in a subject like music? | *Terminology | Slang | Synonyms | Dialect
test: Which word is an example of scientific terminology? | *Photosynthesis | Yummy | Bouncy | Cosy
exam: Why does a teacher ask you to use correct terminology? | *So you use the special words of the subject accurately | So you can talk faster | So your work becomes longer | So you can write in rhymes
